(Interpretation Engine) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
0.118 0.118 0.118 rg
54.0 698.0 moveto
(The interpretation engine is the product's core intellectual property. It runs entirely on-device with no network access and produces a plain-language status, reason, and conservative guidance for each reading.) Tj
/F2 12.0 Tf
0.086 0.314 0.627 rg
54.0 682.0 moveto
(Step 1 -- Baseline-Relative Band Classification) Tj
62.0 666.0 moveto
(Each value is checked against the metric's normal range \(GREEN\), warning buffer \(YELLOW\), or) Tj
62.0 653.0 moveto
(critical threshold \(RED\). The warning buffer is 10% of the normal range span beyond each edge,) Tj
62.0 640.0 moveto
(so it behaves consistently across narrow ranges \(temperature\) and wide ones \(glucose\). Missing) Tj
62.0 627.0 moveto
(or non-finite values are reported as YELLOW with a 'No reading' label.) Tj
/F2 12.0 Tf
0.086 0.314 0.627 rg
54.0 608.0 moveto
(Step 2 -- Trend Downgrade) Tj
62.0 592.0 moveto
(A reading within the normal band that shows a declining trend is escalated to YELLOW, because a) Tj
62.0 579.0 moveto
(downward trajectory inside normal limits still signals deterioration. Trend direction is) Tj
62.0 566.0 moveto
(computed from the rate of change over the most recent readings, with metric-aware polarity) Tj
62.0 553.0 moveto
(\(increasing sleep duration is good; increasing heart rate is not\).) Tj
/F2 12.0 Tf
0.086 0.314 0.627 rg
54.0 534.0 moveto
(Step 3 -- Combined-Signal Escalation) Tj
62.0 518.0 moveto
(If three or more metrics are simultaneously off-nominal within a 24-hour context window, the) Tj
62.0 505.0 moveto
(status of the current reading is escalated one level. This catches clustered abnormalities that) Tj
62.0 492.0 moveto
(indicate systemic issues rather than isolated events.) Tj
/F2 12.0 Tf
0.086 0.314 0.627 rg
54.0 473.0 moveto
(Step 4 -- Plain-Language Reason and Guidance) Tj
62.0 457.0 moveto
(Each classification produces a human-readable reason \(e.g., 'Heart rate is critically above the) Tj
62.0 444.0 moveto
(normal maximum of 100 bpm'\) and metric-specific guidance text. Guidance is conservatively worded) Tj
62.0 431.0 moveto
(for space medicine contexts \(e.g., 'Sit down, stay calm and notify the Medical Officer now.) Tj
62.0 418.0 moveto
(Repeat the reading in 5 minutes' for RED heart rate\).) Tj
54.0 395.0 moveto
(The engine also computes rolling statistics \(mean, median, standard deviation, min, max\)) Tj
54.0 381.0 moveto
(over a sliding window of up to 24 readings, detects rate of change in units per minute, and) Tj
54.0 367.0 moveto
(detects drift beyond two standard deviations from baseline. Trend windows are configurable) Tj
54.0 353.0 moveto
(per metric via the rules schema package.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj

