/F2 13.0 Tf
0.086 0.314 0.627 rg
54.0 698.0 moveto
(FastAPI Backend) Tj
54.0 682.0 moveto
(The ground backend is a FastAPI application with async SQLAlchemy ORM backed by PostgreSQL.) Tj
54.0 668.0 moveto
(It provides REST endpoints for crew reading ingestion, astronaut readings retrieval,) Tj
54.0 654.0 moveto
(baseline computation, achievement awarding, reminder creation, mission control aggregation,) Tj
54.0 640.0 moveto
(and research cohort access. All endpoints are protected by role-based access control) Tj
54.0 626.0 moveto
(dependencies.) Tj
/F2 13.0 Tf
0.086 0.314 0.627 rg
54.0 604.0 moveto
(Security Model) Tj
/F2 11.0 Tf
0.157 0.157 0.157 rg
54.0 588.0 moveto
(API-Key Authentication) Tj
62.0 574.0 moveto
(Service-to-service calls are authenticated via the X-API-Key header with constant-time comparison) Tj
62.0 562.0 moveto
(against the ASTRA_API_KEY environment variable. Constant-time comparison prevents timing) Tj
62.0 550.0 moveto
(side-channel attacks that could leak the key one byte at a time. When ASTRA_API_KEY is not) Tj
62.0 538.0 moveto
(configured, all requests are denied by default -- a missing secret is safe.) Tj
54.0 520.0 moveto
/F2 11.0 Tf
0.157 0.157 0.157 rg
54.0 520.0 moveto
(Role-Based Access Control) Tj
62.0 506.0 moveto
(Six roles \(Astronaut, Medical Officer, Mission Control, Planner, Researcher, Admin\) with permission) Tj
62.0 494.0 moveto
(sets enforced via FastAPI Depends\(\) dependencies. The prototype uses an X-User-Role header for demo) Tj
62.0 482.0 moveto
(purposes; production deployment requires JWT claim verification or mTLS certificate Subject DN) Tj
62.0 470.0 moveto
(mapping. The header-based approach is documented as insecure and must not be used in production.) Tj
54.0 452.0 moveto
/F2 11.0 Tf
0.157 0.157 0.157 rg
54.0 452.0 moveto
(Bundle Verification) Tj
62.0 438.0 moveto
(Inbound DTN sync bundles are verified with Ed25519 signature over a SHA-256 hash of the canonical) Tj
62.0 426.0 moveto
(JSON payload \(sorted keys, no whitespace\). This ensures both integrity \(the hash matches\) and) Tj
62.0 414.0 moveto
(authenticity \(the signature verifies against the trusted public key\). The client in) Tj
62.0 402.0 moveto
(src/lib/crypto.ts and the server in security/keys.py use the same canonicalization convention.) Tj
54.0 384.0 moveto
/F2 11.0 Tf
0.157 0.157 0.157 rg
54.0 384.0 moveto
(Append-Only Audit Log) Tj
62.0 370.0 moveto
(Every significant action \(reading ingestion, achievement award, bundle verification, outbox status) Tj
62.0 358.0 moveto
(change\) is recorded in an append-only audit_events table with astronaut_id, action type, JSON) Tj
62.0 346.0 moveto
(details, and timestamp. The audit log supports compliance auditing and forensic investigation of) Tj
62.0 334.0 moveto
(anomalous activity.) Tj
54.0 316.0 moveto
/F2 11.0 Tf
0.157 0.157 0.157 rg
54.0 316.0 moveto
(Device-Level Encryption) Tj
62.0 302.0 moveto
(AES-256-GCM encryption of all local data with a non-extractable CryptoKey ensures that a stolen or) Tj
62.0 290.0 moveto
(lost device does not expose crew health information. The key is never exported from the browser's) Tj
62.0 278.0 moveto
(key store and cannot be extracted by JavaScript running in the same origin without user interaction.) Tj
54.0 260.0 moveto
ET
endstream
endobj

